DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The GEOM framework has its own event queue to inform classes about impor‐
     tant events.  The event queue can be also used by GEOM classes them‐
     selves, for example to work around some restrictions in the I/O path,
     where sleeping, heavy weight tasks, etc. are not permitted.

     The gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt() function tells the GEOM framework to call function
     _f_u_n_c with argument _a_r_g from the event queue.  The _f_l_a_g argument is passed
     to malloc(9) for memory allocations inside of gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt().  The only
     allowed flags are M_WAITOK and M_NOWAIT.  The rest of the arguments are
     used as references to identify the event.  An event can be canceled by
     using any of the given references as an argument to gg__ccaanncceell__eevveenntt().
     The list of references has to end with a NULL value.

     The gg__wwaaiittffoorr__eevveenntt() function is a blocking version of the
     gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt() function.  It waits until the event is finished or can‐
     celed and then returns.

     The gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt__eepp() function posts the event with a pre-allocated
     _s_t_r_u_c_t _g___e_v_e_n_t.  An event may be pre-allocated with gg__aalllloocc__eevveenntt().

     The gg__ccaanncceell__eevveenntt() function cancels all event(s) identified by _r_e_f.
     Cancellation is equivalent to calling the requested function with re‐
     quested arguments and argument _f_l_a_g set to EV_CANCEL.

RREESSTTRRIICCTTIIOONNSS//CCOONNDDIITTIIOONNSS
     gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt():

           The argument _f_l_a_g has to be M_WAITOK or M_NOWAIT.

           The list of references has to end with a NULL value.

     gg__wwaaiittffoorr__eevveenntt():

           The argument _f_l_a_g has to be M_WAITOK or M_NOWAIT.

           The list of references has to end with a NULL value.

           The gg__wwaaiittffoorr__eevveenntt() function cannot be called from an event,
           since doing so would result in a deadlock.

     gg__aalllloocc__eevveenntt():

           The argument _f_l_a_g has to be M_WAITOK or M_NOWAIT.

           The returned _s_t_r_u_c_t _g___e_v_e_n_t _* must be freed with gg__ffrreeee() if
           gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt__eepp() is not called.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt() and gg__wwaaiittffoorr__eevveenntt() functions return 0 if success‐
     ful; otherwise an error code is returned.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Example of a function called from the event queue.

           void
           example_event(void *arg, int flag)
           {

                   if (flag == EV_CANCEL) {
                           printf("Event with argument %p canceled.\n", arg);
                           return;
                   }

                   printf("Event with argument %p called.\n", arg);
           }

EERRRROORRSS
     Possible errors for the gg__ppoosstt__eevveenntt() function:

     [ENOMEM]           The _f_l_a_g argument was set to M_NOWAIT and there was
                        insufficient memory.

     Possible errors for the gg__wwaaiittffoorr__eevveenntt() function:

     [EAGAIN]           The event was canceled.

     [ENOMEM]           The _f_l_a_g argument was set to M_NOWAIT and there was
                        insufficient memory.

